    "title": "Comprehensive Evidence-Based Postpartum Depression Screening Protocol for Doulas Serving Medicaid and Vulnerable Populations",
    "domain": "Maternal Mental Health",
    "role": "Doula",
    "description": "This protocol outlines an evidence-based approach for doulas to conduct postpartum depression (PPD) screening among Medicaid and vulnerable populations. It emphasizes early identification, culturally sensitive support, and appropriate referral pathways to improve maternal mental health outcomes.",
    "measurement": "Process metrics will include the percentage of postpartum individuals screened for PPD by doulas, the completion rate of screening tools (e.g., EPDS, PHQ-9), and the rate of successful referrals to mental health services. Outcome metrics will involve tracking the proportion of individuals who receive follow-up care after a positive screen, changes in PPD symptom severity scores over time, and client satisfaction with the screening and referral process.",
